{
  "title": "Attention in a transformer",
  "slug": "attention-in-a-transformer",
  "hue": 268,
  "lede": "Self-attention lets every word in a sentence look at every other word and decide how much each one matters, all at once. It is the core of the transformer.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "kind": "experience",
      "heading": "Where each word looks",
      "body": "<style>\n.at{box-sizing:border-box;max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;gap:18px;grid-template-columns:1fr;font-family:var(--ow-font);color:var(--ow-fg)}\n.at *{box-sizing:border-box}\n@media (min-width:780px){.at{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.55fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:26px;align-items:start}}\n.at-q{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;font-weight:600}\n.at-q b{color:var(--ow-accent)}\n.at-heads{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin:0 0 6px}\n.at-chip{appearance:none;font:inherit;font-size:14px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;min-height:38px;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:999px;border:1.5px solid var(--ow-line);background:var(--ow-bg);color:var(--ow-fg);cursor:pointer;touch-action:manipulation}\n.at-chip small{font-size:12px;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.at-chip[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:var(--ow-fg);border-color:var(--ow-fg);color:var(--ow-bg)}\n.at-chip[aria-pressed=\"true\"] small{color:color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-bg) 75%,transparent)}\n.at-stage{position:relative;border-radius:18px;background:var(--ow-panel);border:1px solid var(--ow-line);padding:6px 10px 12px}\n.at-arcs{display:block;width:100%;height:210px;overflow:visible}\n.at-arcs path{fill:none;stroke:var(--ow-accent);stroke-linecap:round;transition:stroke-width .25s ease,opacity .25s ease}\n.at-toks{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(8,minmax(0,1fr));gap:4px}\n.at-tok{appearance:none;font:inherit;min-width:0;padding:7px 0 6px;border-radius:10px;border:1.5px solid transparent;background:transparent;color:var(--ow-fg);cursor:pointer;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:5px;touch-action:manipulation}\n.at-tok b{font-size:clamp(11px,2.6vw,16px);font-weight:650;white-space:nowrap}\n.at-tok i{display:block;width:78%;height:5px;border-radius:9px;background:color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-line) 80%,transparent);overflow:hidden}\n.at-tok i span{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--ow-accent);border-radius:9px;transition:width .25s ease}\n.at-tok em{font-style:normal;font-family:var(--ow-mono);font-size:clamp(10px,2.2vw,12.5px);color:var(--ow-muted);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.at-tok[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{border-color:var(--ow-accent);background:color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-accent) 12%,transparent)}\n.at-tok[aria-pressed=\"true\"] em{color:var(--ow-accent);font-weight:600}\n.at button:focus-visible,.at input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-accent) 55%,transparent);outline-offset:2px}\n.at-say{margin:12px 2px 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.4;min-height:2.8em}\n.at-say b{color:var(--ow-accent)}\n.at-box{padding:14px 16px;border-radius:14px;border:1px solid var(--ow-line);background:var(--ow-panel)}\n.at-box+.at-box{margin-top:12px}\n.at-lab{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;font-size:15px;font-weight:600}\n.at-lab output{font-family:var(--ow-mono);color:var(--ow-muted);font-weight:500;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.at input[type=range]{width:100%;margin:8px 0 2px;height:28px;accent-color:var(--ow-accent);cursor:pointer}\n.at-ends{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.at-h{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:13px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.at-map{display:grid;max-width:300px;grid-template-columns:auto repeat(8,minmax(0,1fr));gap:2px;font-size:11.5px;align-items:center}\n.at-map .rl{padding-right:6px;text-align:right;color:var(--ow-muted);white-space:nowrap;cursor:pointer}\n.at-map .rl.on{color:var(--ow-accent);font-weight:700}\n.at-map .cl{writing-mode:vertical-rl;transform:rotate(180deg);color:var(--ow-muted);text-align:left;height:44px;justify-self:center}\n.at-map .c{aspect-ratio:1;border-radius:3px;cursor:pointer;background:color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-accent) calc(var(--w)*100%),var(--ow-bg))}\n.at-map .c.on{box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--ow-fg)}\n.at-key{margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.at-key code{font-family:var(--ow-mono);font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ow-fg)}\n@media (max-width:420px){.at-stage{padding:4px 4px 10px}.at-arcs{height:150px}.at-q{font-size:17px}.at-toks{gap:1px}}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.at-arcs path,.at-tok i span{transition:none}}\n</style>\n<div class=\"at\">\n  <div>\n    <p class=\"at-q\">Click a word to see <b>which words it pays attention to</b>.</p>\n    <div class=\"at-heads\" id=\"at-heads\" aria-label=\"Attention head\"></div>\n    <div class=\"at-stage\">\n      <svg class=\"at-arcs\" id=\"at-svg\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></svg>\n      <div class=\"at-toks\" id=\"at-toks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Sentence: pick the word doing the looking\"></div>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"at-say\" id=\"at-say\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"at-box\">\n      <label class=\"at-lab\" for=\"at-t\"><span>Softmax temperature</span><output id=\"at-to\" for=\"at-t\">1.0</output></label>\n      <input id=\"at-t\" type=\"range\" min=\"-2\" max=\"2\" step=\"0.05\" value=\"0\">\n      <div class=\"at-ends\"><span>sharp: one word wins</span><span>flat: all equal</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"at-box\">\n      <p class=\"at-h\">Every word at once, this head</p>\n      <div class=\"at-map\" id=\"at-map\" aria-label=\"Attention weights: rows are the word looking, columns the word looked at\"></div>\n      <p class=\"at-key\">Weights are <code>softmax(score &divide; temperature)</code>, so each row sums to 100%. The scores are <b>hand-picked to illustrate</b> patterns real heads learn; they are not from a trained model.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var W=['The','animal','was','too','tired','so','it','slept'];\n  function grid(pairs){var m=[];for(var i=0;i<8;i++){m.push([0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0])}pairs.forEach(function(p){m[p[0]][p[1]]=p[2]});return m}\n  var prev=[];for(var i=0;i<8;i++){prev.push([i,i,1]);if(i)prev.push([i,i-1,3.2]);else prev[0][2]=3}\n  var heads=[\n    {name:'Head 1',tag:'previous word',m:grid(prev),say:'looks mostly one step back, a simple position pattern many heads learn.'},\n    {name:'Head 2',tag:'who is it about?',m:grid([[0,1,2.5],[0,0,1],[1,1,2],[1,0,1.2],[2,1,2.5],[2,2,.5],[3,4,1.5],[3,1,1],[4,1,2.5],[4,2,1],[5,1,1.2],[5,4,1.2],[5,5,.4],[6,1,3.6],[6,0,1.2],[6,6,.5],[7,6,2.4],[7,1,2.4]]),say:'links words to the thing the sentence is about, so “it” can pick up the meaning of “animal”.'},\n    {name:'Head 3',tag:'what describes it?',m:grid([[0,1,2],[1,4,2.6],[1,2,1],[2,4,2],[3,4,3],[4,3,2.5],[4,4,1],[5,4,2.5],[5,7,1.6],[6,4,2.6],[6,2,1],[7,4,2],[7,5,2]]),say:'connects words to their description and cause, so “it” also gathers “tired”.'}\n  ];\n  var head=1,sel=6,T=1;\n  var svg=document.getElementById('at-svg'),toks=document.getElementById('at-toks'),say=document.getElementById('at-say'),map=document.getElementById('at-map'),hb=document.getElementById('at-heads'),R=document.getElementById('at-t');\n  function soft(row){var mx=-1e9,i,e=[],s=0;for(i=0;i<8;i++)mx=Math.max(mx,row[i]/T);for(i=0;i<8;i++){e[i]=Math.exp(row[i]/T-mx);s+=e[i]}return e.map(function(x){return x/s})}\n  function pct(w){var p=w*100;return p>=9.95?Math.round(p)+'%':p>=0.95?p.toFixed(1)+'%':'<1%'}\n  heads.forEach(function(h,k){var b=document.createElement('button');b.type='button';b.className='at-chip';b.innerHTML=h.name+' <small>'+h.tag+'</small>';b.addEventListener('click',function(){head=k;render()});h.btn=b;hb.appendChild(b)});\n  var tb=W.map(function(w,k){\n    var b=document.createElement('button');b.type='button';b.className='at-tok';b.innerHTML='<b>'+w+'</b><i><span></span></i><em></em>';\n    b.addEventListener('click',function(){sel=k;render()});\n    b.addEventListener('keydown',function(e){var d=e.key==='ArrowRight'?1:e.key==='ArrowLeft'?-1:0;if(d){e.preventDefault();sel=(sel+d+8)%8;render();tb[sel].focus()}});\n    toks.appendChild(b);return b});\n  var corner=document.createElement('span');map.appendChild(corner);\n  W.forEach(function(w){var c=document.createElement('span');c.className='cl';c.textContent=w;map.appendChild(c)});\n  var cells=[],rls=[];\n  W.forEach(function(w,r){\n    var l=document.createElement('span');l.className='rl';l.textContent=w;l.addEventListener('click',function(){sel=r;render()});map.appendChild(l);rls.push(l);\n    cells.push(W.map(function(_,c){var d=document.createElement('span');d.className='c';d.addEventListener('click',function(){sel=r;render()});map.appendChild(d);return d}));\n  });\n  var NS='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';\n  function arcs(w){\n    while(svg.firstChild)svg.removeChild(svg.firstChild);\n    var sb=svg.getBoundingClientRect(),H=sb.height||190,base=H-4,xs=tb.map(function(b){var r=b.getBoundingClientRect();return r.left-sb.left+r.width/2});\n    var sx=xs[sel],maxH=H-14,span=Math.max(1,sb.width||600);\n    var order=w.map(function(v,i){return i}).sort(function(a,b){return w[a]-w[b]});\n    order.forEach(function(j){\n      var v=w[j],p=document.createElementNS(NS,'path'),d;\n      if(j===sel){var r=Math.min(26,(xs[1]-xs[0])*.45||20);d='M'+(sx-r*.6)+' '+base+'C'+(sx-r*1.3)+' '+(base-r*2.4)+' '+(sx+r*1.3)+' '+(base-r*2.4)+' '+(sx+r*.6)+' '+base}\n      else{var tx=xs[j],h=Math.min(maxH,24+Math.abs(tx-sx)/span*H*1.7);d='M'+sx+' '+base+'C'+sx+' '+(base-h*1.33)+' '+tx+' '+(base-h*1.33)+' '+tx+' '+base}\n      p.setAttribute('d',d);p.style.strokeWidth=(1+v*18).toFixed(2)+'px';p.style.opacity=(.12+.88*Math.sqrt(v)).toFixed(3);\n      svg.appendChild(p);\n      var c=document.createElementNS(NS,'circle');c.setAttribute('cx',j===sel?sx:xs[j]);c.setAttribute('cy',base);c.setAttribute('r',(2+v*5).toFixed(2));c.setAttribute('fill','var(--ow-accent)');c.style.opacity=(.3+.7*Math.sqrt(v)).toFixed(3);svg.appendChild(c);\n    });\n  }\n  function render(){\n    var h=heads[head],w=soft(h.m[sel]);\n    heads.forEach(function(x,k){x.btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(k===head))});\n    tb.forEach(function(b,k){b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(k===sel));b.querySelector('i span').style.width=(w[k]*100).toFixed(1)+'%';b.querySelector('em').textContent=pct(w[k]);b.setAttribute('aria-label',W[k]+(k===sel?', looking: ':', ')+pct(w[k])+' of the attention of '+W[sel])});\n    for(var r=0;r<8;r++){var rw=soft(h.m[r]);rls[r].className='rl'+(r===sel?' on':'');for(var c=0;c<8;c++){cells[r][c].style.setProperty('--w',Math.min(1,rw[c]*1.25).toFixed(3));cells[r][c].className='c'+(r===sel?' on':'');cells[r][c].title=W[r]+' → '+W[c]+': '+pct(rw[c])}}\n    var best=0;for(var j=1;j<8;j++)if(w[j]>w[best])best=j;\n    var spread=w.filter(function(v){return v>=0.1}).length;\n    say.innerHTML='<b>“'+W[sel]+'”</b> gives <b>'+pct(w[best])+'</b> of its attention to “'+W[best]+'”'+(spread>2?', and spreads the rest over '+(spread-1)+' more words':'')+'. '+h.name+' '+h.say;\n    arcs(w);\n  }\n  R.addEventListener('input',function(){T=Math.pow(2,+R.value);var t=T<1?T.toFixed(2):T.toFixed(1);document.getElementById('at-to').textContent=t;R.setAttribute('aria-valuetext','temperature '+t);render()});\n  if(window.ResizeObserver)new ResizeObserver(function(){render()}).observe(svg);else window.addEventListener('resize',render);\n  render();\n})();\n</script>\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "Queries, keys and values",
      "body": "An attention function maps a query and a set of key-value pairs to an output [1]. Each word gets a query, a key and a value vector [2], and its score for another word is the dot product of its query with that word's key [3]. The scores are divided by the square root of the key size, then a softmax turns them into weights [4] that are positive and add up to 1 [5]. The output is the weighted sum of the values [6].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), full text on arXiv",
          "quote": "An attention function can be described as mapping a query and a set of key-value pairs to an output"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://jalammar.github.io/illustrated-transformer/",
          "title": "The Illustrated Transformer (Jay Alammar)",
          "quote": "So for each word, we create a Query vector, a Key vector, and a Value vector."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://jalammar.github.io/illustrated-transformer/",
          "title": "The Illustrated Transformer (Jay Alammar)",
          "quote": "The score is calculated by taking the dot product of the query vector with the key vector of the respective word"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), full text on arXiv",
          "quote": "and apply a softmax function to obtain the weights on the values"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://jalammar.github.io/illustrated-transformer/",
          "title": "The Illustrated Transformer (Jay Alammar)",
          "quote": "Softmax normalizes the scores so they’re all positive and add up to 1."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), full text on arXiv",
          "quote": "The output is computed as a weighted sum of the values"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "Many heads at once",
      "body": "The original Transformer runs 8 attention heads side by side, each with its own query, key and value weights [1][2]. Several heads let the model attend to different kinds of information at different positions [3]. In Jay Alammar's walkthrough, while encoding \"it\", one head focuses most on \"the animal\" and another on \"tired\" [4], the two patterns the heads above imitate.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), full text on arXiv",
          "quote": "parallel attention layers, or heads"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://jalammar.github.io/illustrated-transformer/",
          "title": "The Illustrated Transformer (Jay Alammar)",
          "quote": "eight attention heads, so we end up with eight sets for each encoder/decoder"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), full text on arXiv",
          "quote": "Multi-head attention allows the model to jointly attend to information from different representation subspaces at different positions."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://jalammar.github.io/illustrated-transformer/",
          "title": "The Illustrated Transformer (Jay Alammar)",
          "quote": "one attention head is focusing most on \"the animal\", while another is focusing on \"tired\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "heading": "Why it replaced recurrence",
      "body": "A recurrent network reads one position after another, and that sequential nature precludes parallelization within a training example [1]. A self-attention layer connects all positions in a constant number of sequential steps, where a recurrent layer needs O(n) [2]. The 2017 paper dropped recurrence entirely [3]; its models trained faster and reached 28.4 BLEU on English-to-German translation [4]. With no recurrence, word order comes from sine and cosine waves of different frequencies [5], a cousin of the [[Fourier transform]].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), full text on arXiv",
          "quote": "sequential nature precludes parallelization within training examples"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), full text on arXiv",
          "quote": "connects all positions with a constant number of sequentially executed operations, whereas a recurrent layer requires"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), arXiv abstract",
          "quote": "dispensing with recurrence and convolutions entirely"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), arXiv abstract",
          "quote": "Our model achieves 28.4 BLEU on the WMT 2014 English-to-German translation task"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7",
          "title": "Attention Is All You Need (Vaswani et al., 2017), full text on arXiv",
          "quote": "sine and cosine functions of different frequencies"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "figure",
      "heading": "One word, four steps",
      "body": "<style>\n.af{box-sizing:border-box;max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;font-family:var(--ow-font);color:var(--ow-fg);display:grid;gap:10px;grid-template-columns:1fr}\n.af *{box-sizing:border-box}\n@media (min-width:720px){.af{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px}}\n.af-c{position:relative;padding:14px 14px 12px;border-radius:14px;background:var(--ow-panel);border:1px solid var(--ow-line)}\n.af-n{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ow-accent);color:var(--ow-accent-ink);font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin-right:8px}\n.af-t{margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center}\n.af-s{margin:4px 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--ow-muted);line-height:1.35;min-height:2.7em}\n.af ol{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:6px}\n.af li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px minmax(0,1fr) 46px;gap:8px;align-items:center;font-size:13.5px}\n.af .w{color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.af .tr{height:10px;border-radius:9px;background:color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-line) 70%,transparent);overflow:hidden}\n.af .tr i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:9px;background:var(--ow-accent)}\n.af .vv{height:14px;border-radius:4px;background:color-mix(in oklch,var(--ow-accent) calc(var(--w)*100%),var(--ow-bg));border:1px solid var(--ow-line)}\n.af .v{font-family:var(--ow-mono);font-size:12.5px;text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.af-foot{grid-column:1/-1;margin:2px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--ow-muted);line-height:1.45}\n@media (min-width:720px){.af-c:not(:last-of-type)::after{content:\"→\";position:absolute;right:-13px;top:14px;font-size:16px;color:var(--ow-muted)}}\n</style>\n<div class=\"af\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scaled dot-product attention for the word it: scores 25.6, 15.2, 3.2 and 8.8 are divided by 8, softmax turns them into 69, 19, 4 and 8 percent, and the output mixes the value vectors with those weights\">\n<div class=\"af-c\"><p class=\"af-t\"><span class=\"af-n\">1</span>Score</p><p class=\"af-s\">query of “it” · key of each word</p><ol><li><span class=\"w\">animal</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:100.0%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">25.6</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">tired</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:59.4%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">15.2</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">so</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:12.5%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">3.2</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">it</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:34.4%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">8.8</span></li></ol></div>\n<div class=\"af-c\"><p class=\"af-t\"><span class=\"af-n\">2</span>Scale</p><p class=\"af-s\">divide by √64 = 8</p><ol><li><span class=\"w\">animal</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:100.0%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">3.2</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">tired</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:59.4%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">1.9</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">so</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:12.5%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">0.4</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">it</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:34.4%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">1.1</span></li></ol></div>\n<div class=\"af-c\"><p class=\"af-t\"><span class=\"af-n\">3</span>Softmax</p><p class=\"af-s\">positive, sums to 100%</p><ol><li><span class=\"w\">animal</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:100.0%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">69%</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">tired</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:27.3%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">19%</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">so</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:6.1%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">4%</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">it</span><span class=\"tr\"><i style=\"width:12.2%\"></i></span><span class=\"v\">8%</span></li></ol></div>\n<div class=\"af-c\"><p class=\"af-t\"><span class=\"af-n\">4</span>Mix</p><p class=\"af-s\">output = Σ weight × value</p><ol><li><span class=\"w\">animal</span><span class=\"vv\" style=\"--w:0.687\"></span><span class=\"v\">×0.69</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">tired</span><span class=\"vv\" style=\"--w:0.187\"></span><span class=\"v\">×0.19</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">so</span><span class=\"vv\" style=\"--w:0.042\"></span><span class=\"v\">×0.04</span></li><li><span class=\"w\">it</span><span class=\"vv\" style=\"--w:0.084\"></span><span class=\"v\">×0.08</span></li></ol></div>\n<p class=\"af-foot\">One head, one word. Illustrative numbers; 64 is the key size per head in the original paper. Every word does this for every other word at the same time.</p>\n</div>"
